cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this project, cite it as a software repository."
title: "FaceAuth Attendance: real-time multi-camera face authentication and attendance backend"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Seyed Mohammad Sina
    family-names: Hosseini
repository-code: "https://github.com/seyedmohammadsinahosseini/cpp-face-auth-attendance"
abstract: >-
  A C++20 backend for face-based presence and attendance on a local network of IP
  cameras. It discovers cameras (V4L2, ONVIF, RTSP), streams them through an
  OpenCV/GStreamer pipeline, runs NVIDIA TensorRT face and head detection, tracks
  identities with ByteTrack, recognises people with a FAISS IndexFlatIP over
  512-dimensional face embeddings, and records arrivals, departures, work
  sessions, tardiness and locations into SQLite, exposed through 56 REST
  endpoints and a 71-function C FFI. Model weights and the proprietary logging
  dependency are intentionally not distributed.
keywords:
  - face-recognition
  - attendance-system
  - tensorrt
  - faiss
  - bytetrack
  - onvif
  - rtsp
  - gstreamer
  - opencv
  - cpp20
  - computer-vision
  - edge-ai
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
